      "description": "Built in 1903 to designs by Hemenway & Miller for the Italian Swiss Colony, the wine company Andrea Sbarboro founded in 1881 as a cooperative with its vineyards at Asti, near Cloverdale; its Battery and Greenwich Street fronts recall an Italian palazzo. It is one of the few warehouses left on the northern waterfront.",
